    {
      "id": "claim_ce0538da83fd4dfd83c074eb20f6f4c1",
      "statement": "pcie_template_accel.sv exposes a BAR0 register map with every register on an 8-byte stride (ID at 0x0000, VERSION 0x0008, SCRATCH 0x0010, COUNTER 0x0018, DMA_SRC 0x0020, DMA_DST 0x0028, DMA_LEN 0x0030, CTRL 0x0038, STATUS 0x0040, IRQ_ACK 0x0048) plus a 4KiB scratchpad RAM at 0x1000-0x1FFF, because Axi4SlaveEngine is LSB-aligned while a strict AXI4 requester is byte-lane-aligned and the two conventions only agree on beat-boundary-aligned accesses.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://examples/pcie_template_accel/pcie_template_accel.sv#L18-L44",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:7d080e7887fd38ac7e68158246d4878b618180472b056f1fadd66119f32bdbfd:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_25344194f20445c1ab702f837e4fc07d",
      "statement": "pcie_template_accel.sv's DMA engine copies DMA_LEN bytes SRC->DST as single-beat 8-byte read/write pairs tagging reads with AXI ID 0 and writes with AXI ID 1, specifically to exercise both of Axi4MasterEngine's per-ID queues, with a trailing partial word written via a masked WSTRB.",
      "evidence": [
